1. DeepSeek-Bot — https://github.com/Fei2411/DeepSeek-Bot
   Copyright (c) 2026 Fei2411
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

   This app is a client for it. Taken from that project:

     · the client channel `POST /api/bot` with the `{endpoint, payload}` /
       `{ok, value}` envelope            (ds-bot/src/client/api.js,
                                          ds-bot/src/host/channel.js)
     · the endpoint names and payloads   (ds-bot/src/host/channel.js)
     · the team view shape               (channel.js — view() and live())
     · the chat item kinds               (ds-bot/src/host/parts.js — displayItems)
     · the approval shape and the
       `allow` / `reject` choices        (ds-bot/src/host/approvals.js)
     · the login-URL token → signed
       cookie handshake                  (app/src/main.mjs, docker/README.md)

   No source file from DeepSeek-Bot is copied into this repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. grok-build-ios — https://github.com/Pedroshakoor/grok-build-ios
   Copyright (c) 2026 Pedro Shakour
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

   The iOS client skeleton comes from it:

     · Sources/Ported/MarkdownLite.swift      copied, unchanged
     · Sources/Ported/PromptBar.swift         adapted (placeholder, enablement,
                                              model line, send affordance)
     · Sources/Ported/PermissionBanner.swift  adapted (DS Bot approvals instead of
                                              ACP session/request_permission)
     · Sources/Ported/DSBTheme.swift          adapted from Theme.swift; the token
                                              names are Grok's, the palette and the
                                              JSON theme loading are not
     · Sources/Models/Chrome.swift            AppScreen / ConnectionPhase /
                                              PermissionOption vocabulary from
                                              Models/ScrollbackEntry.swift
     · Sources/TeamModel.swift                the observable surface (screen,
                                              messages, draft, connectionPhase,
                                              permissionRequest, theme) follows
                                              AppModel.swift

   No ACP, WebSocket, companion bridge or Grok theme JSON is included: that half of
   the project is replaced by DeepSeek Bot's HTTP channel.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. DeepSeek Harness (dsh) — https://github.com/deepseek-ai/dsh

   The host this client talks to. Not bundled, not vendored. The app is inert until
   you point it at a `dsh` host you run yourself.

